  "result": "Full independent visual coverage completed on these exact canonical bytes. All source and battle thirteen raw clips, five face and two body views at six fresh phases were personally seen. Eyes, beak, cream cheeks and chin remain coherent; wings, torso, hips, legs, talons and feather tail stay connected. The dark scarf has an unresolved shape change: raw attack .28 compresses it into a thin strip beneath the lower beak while cream throat/chest elongates; attack .48 expands it into a broad rounded dark bib covering the raised throat. Under-front .28 shows an uneven lateral scarf edge. Cast tilted-up poses show a milder expansion. All low/medium transition rows were reviewed, including strike onset .025/.05/.10 where the expanded dark bib is also conspicuous. All216 actual battle technique frames were reviewed: Wind Strike and Wind Breaker .24/.36 show the compressed strip, and .48 the expanded bib. Full native Wind Strike front .36/.48 and side .48 retain this appearance. This remains a bounded ownership/rigging concern, not a claim of topology tearing. Idle24 and atlas16 personally viewed; those scopes retain coherent anatomy.",
